course: dictionary
lesson: 2507
title: Decay: rot and breakdown
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so use the clues around it. «Sugary and fizzy drinks cause tooth decay, so water and milk are the best everyday drinks.» The drinks cause something bad to teeth, and water and milk are the good choices. So decay here means damage that spoils teeth.
explain: Decay can also be a process. In science, dead plants and animals decay, which means they rot and break down slowly. Ask yourself what fits: the word that makes sense in «a hole in a tooth caused by decay» is the damage itself, and the hole is called a cavity.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If you put in rot or break down slowly and the sentence still makes sense, you have it right. If you put in grow or shine and it sounds silly, try again.
fact: Decay means to rot or break down slowly.
fact: Decay can also mean to become weaker or worse over time, like an old building.
fact: Tooth decay is holes in teeth caused by germs and sugar.
fact: «Tooth decay» is the most common long-lasting disease of children, and it is almost always preventable.
fact: Decomposers such as fungi, bacteria and worms make dead things decay, returning nutrients to the soil.
exercise: «Sugary and fizzy drinks cause tooth decay, so water and milk are the best everyday drinks.» What is tooth decay? | A kind of toothbrush | Shiny, clean teeth after a good meal | A sweet drink made with fizzy water | *Holes in teeth caused by germs and sugar
exercise: In science, worms and fungi help dead plants to decay. What does decay mean here? | To grow very quickly and strongly | *To rot and break down slowly | To become bright and shiny | To freeze solid
exercise: «A hole in a tooth caused by decay is called a cavity.» Find and copy one word that means a hole in a tooth. | caused | tooth | *cavity | decay
test: An old wooden fence that is slowly falling apart is in decay. What does decay suggest? | Growing taller each year | Being made new | Being painted bright red | *Becoming weaker and worse over time
test: «Tooth decay (dentists call it caries) is the most common long-lasting disease of children.» Which word do dentists use for tooth decay? | Sugar | Germ | *Caries | Cavity
exam: Brushing your teeth twice a day helps to stop ___ from forming. | *decay | Milk | Sugar | Water
